diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index f1b273b..c87050f 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -64,3 +64,13 @@ Room Membership Rules:
   - Bypasses `ActionDispatch` form parameter parsing for non-multipart requests so `curl -d "..."` raw bodies (including `%`, `&`, etc.) are read directly from `request.raw_post` as UTF-8.
   - Validates that the message has a non-blank body or attachment (`422 Unprocessable Content`).
   - Broadcasts the message and triggers unread room updates and Web Push notifications identically to human-authored messages, returning `201 Created` with `Location: /messages/:message_id`.
+
+## Bots per Member Limit
+
+- `Account` defines `has_delegated_json :settings, restrict_room_creation_to_administrators: false, bots_per_member: 5` (`Account::DEFAULT_BOTS_PER_MEMBER = 5`).
+- Administrators can configure "Bots per member" on `/account/edit` (`AccountsController#edit` / `AccountsController#update`).
+- `User#bot_limit_reached?` (`!administrator? && bots.active.count >= Current.account.settings.bots_per_member`):
+  - Counts only active bots created by the member (`bots.active.count`), so deleted/deactivated bots do not count.
+  - Administrators are never limited.
+  - Lowering the limit keeps existing bots active and editable; it only blocks creating new bots (`validate :ensure_creator_within_bot_limit, on: :create, if: :bot?` and `BotsController` `before_action :ensure_within_bot_limit, only: %i[ new create ]`).
+  - When `Current.user.bot_limit_reached?` is true on `/bots`, the "Add a chat bot" button is replaced with a notice telling the member they've "reached the limit", and direct `GET /bots/new` or `POST /bots` requests return `403 Forbidden`.
